 the terminal-yet-unreadable window (given sidecar.emit() already runs synchronously inside work() before the terminal record_gate_run in finally) — is it emit()'s return vs. cross-store readability of the event? — and scope the fix to that layer, rather than assuming gate_runs index ordering is the cause.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.1,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan Scope: 'src/rebar/llm/gate_runs.py (the run index that gate_status replays) and the plan-review sidecar write path. Either the terminal transition waits on the sidecar write, or gate_status exposes whether this job's sidecar is readable yet.'","_mcp_llm.py:164-179 — work() (review_plan) runs, THEN record_gate_run(terminal) in finally; the sidecar emit is inside review_plan and returns before finally.","plan_review/__init__.py:564-579 — sidecar.emit(...) is a synchronous call within the review body.","ABSENCE: the plan gives no account of WHY an already-emitted sidecar is not readable at terminal time (git commit visibility / cross-process store view), which is the actual gap the repro exhibits."],"finding":"The plan scopes the fix to the gate_runs run-index/status ordering, but in the actual code the REVIEW_RESULT sidecar is emitted synchronously inside review_plan() (the daemon's work()) at plan_review/__init__.py:564-579, and work() returns BEFORE the daemon's finally records the terminal gate_run entry (_mcp_llm.py:159-180). The sidecar write already strictly precedes the terminal index write in-process, so 'deferring the terminal transition until the sidecar write' does not by itself close the observed window — the reproduction's terminal-yet-absent-sidecar condition implies the real cause is a durability/visibility layer below emit() (event-append/commit to the tickets tracker or the reader's view of it), which the plan neither diagnoses nor scopes.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f4eedc2c4b911f75e","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Scope section; Reproduction step 3; src/rebar/_mcp_llm.py:159-180; src/rebar/llm/plan_review/__init__.py:564-579","norm_id":"ned1932cc38df2d61","priority":0.9,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A fix that only ensures work() returned (emit called) before terminal status would still leave the repro's window open, because emit-called != sidecar-readable-by-the-reader."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Define the readable-indicator as an actual read of this job's REVIEW_RESULT sidecar by its event id (readability = the observable the AC demands), independent of any assumption that the writer's return implies visibility; confirm via the repro's real timing whether emit() had returned when gate_status read terminal.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.9,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"omits_required_site","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"high","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Make the test model the ACTUAL window — writer returned / terminal status recorded but sidecar not yet readable by the reader — rather than a writer held open (which, given emit() is synchronous inside work(), would also block the terminal transition and not reproduce the observed sequence).","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.1,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Testing: 'with a stubbed sidecar writer ... driving the window explicitly ... by controlling the writer rather than by timing.'","Reproduction: terminal 'passed'/'verdict' were observed (writer returned) while the prior run's sidecar was newest — i.e. the current run's sidecar was written LATER, not merely 'held open'.","Given emit() is synchronous inside work() and precedes the terminal record, 'held open' would block work() itself and thus block the terminal status — which is not the observed sequence."],"finding":"The Testing/AC plan reproduces the race with 'a stubbed sidecar writer held open', modeling a writer that has NOT returned. But the reproduction's window is AFTER the writer returned (verdict computed, terminal status recorded) yet BEFORE the sidecar is readable. A held-open-writer stub may not faithfully exercise the observed condition, so the tests could pass while the real window remains.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fa0353ee5861a9cea","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Testing section; Acceptance Criteria bullets 1-2","norm_id":"n595c61ba779abc9c","priority":0.9,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["The stubbed-writer-held-open test asserts non-readability during a state that cannot actually coexist with a terminal record in production, giving false confidence."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.9,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"contradicts_reality","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"high","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Define and test the terminal-but-write-failed case: gate_status must surface a distinguishable not-durable/failed indicator (not merely not-yet-readable), so a polling caller can stop and act rather than loop forever.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5b","T5e"],"criteria":["T5b","E6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":0.05,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["The plan preserves best-effort sidecar recording (Non-goals) but only describes the transient race window (writer 'held open' then 'released') in Testing and ACs.","ACs cover 'sidecar not yet written' and 'sidecar written' but not 'sidecar write failed and will never land.'","Under the expose-readability option a permanently-failed write leaves the readability indicator false forever, so a poll-then-read caller loops indefinitely with no timeout, degraded-mode, or error surfaced."],"finding":"Neither proposed solution specifies behavior when the best-effort sidecar write PERMANENTLY fails, leaving an unbounded/unsurfaced failure path.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f69c4ce6b353a6bb0","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Scope / Acceptance Criteria","norm_id":"n4764f4dd4346dee1","priority":1.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Disk/IO error on the sidecar write; the caller polls gate_status forever waiting for a sidecar that will never appear."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Add an AC exercising a stubbed writer that ERRORS (not just held open), asserting gate_status reports the verdict terminal with an explicit non-transient not-readable/failed state and that the failure is logged.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"uncertifiable_outcome","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State the disposition for the permanent-sidecar-write-failure arm: define whether the not-yet-readable indicator is transient (retryable — keep polling) vs terminal-unavailable (fatal — findings were dropped best-effort and will never land), so a poll-then-read caller cannot spin forever.","cohort":["E3","E5","G5","T12","T6","T9","necessity","project.failure-disposition-contract","project.portability"],"criteria":["project.failure-disposition-contract"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":0.1,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Non-goal: 'Making sidecar recording non-best-effort in a way that would fail a run whose findings failed to persist; the verdict must still be reported.'","AC1: 'either it is not yet terminal, or the response carries an explicit not-yet-readable indicator' — carries a transient/retryable connotation but never names the permanent-failure disposition.","ABSENCE: no disposition word (transient/retryable vs fatal/permanent) attached to the case where the best-effort sidecar write is dropped and never becomes readable."],"finding":"The plan states a disposition for the sidecar-not-yet-written arm (either 'not yet terminal' or an 'explicit not-yet-readable indicator') but does not distinguish a TRANSIENT not-yet-durable state (retryable — the write is in flight, poll again) from a PERMANENT write failure (fatal — best-effort recording dropped the sidecar and it will never appear). Because a non-goal explicitly keeps sidecar recording best-effort ('Making sidecar recording non-best-effort ... the verdict must still be reported'), a permanently-failed write is a real arm. A caller following the poll-then-read loop against a 'not-yet-readable' indicator would then poll forever for findings that will never land.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fdc01be0ea1aa8a86","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Scope / Non-goals / Acceptance Criteria AC1","norm_id":"nc068d1286ef5021f","priority":1.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A run whose REVIEW_RESULT write fails (disk/tracker error) under best-effort recording: gate_status reports terminal-but-not-readable indefinitely, and a caller looping poll-then-read waits for findings that will never appear."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Give the readability indicator (or the deferred-terminal path) a bounded/terminal exhaustion state — e.g. distinguish 'pending' (retryable) from 'unavailable' (best-effort write dropped) — and add a pytest that drives the writer to fail permanently and asserts gate_status reaches a distinguishable, non-looping state rather than an indefinite not-yet-readable.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"uncertifiable_outcome","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State the name/type/values of the sidecar-readability field on the gate_status response (e.g. a `findings_readable: bool` or a `findings` durability sub-block) so the AC's field assertion is concrete.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5b","T5e"],"criteria":["E2"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.36,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["AC1: 'the response carries an explicit not-yet-readable indicator; verified by pytest ... asserting the returned fields.'","The response field name/shape and its readable/not-readable values are unstated, though the existing 'durable' block is named for contrast."],"finding":"The 'explicit not-yet-readable indicator' referenced in AC1 has no stated field name, type, or value set.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f328d626b1bfc5f8b","impact":0.44,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria (first bullet)","norm_id":"n6a03c87cfd5e4830","priority":0.44,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Two implementers or the test author must invent the field name/shape, risking test-vs-impl drift."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"underspecified_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":null,"blocking_enabled":null,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["P6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":null,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["1 criterion line(s) bundle multiple deliverables with 'and' (split so each is independently verifiable)."],"finding":"Acceptance-criteria / definition-of-done quality issues.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f607dd457c67f9209","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"ned06ebc801a522e3","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Split compound criteria, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Reconcile the 'defer terminal transition' option with the Non-goal 'the verdict must still be reported': either bound the defer with a fallback that still reports the verdict on sidecar-write failure, or drop the defer option as incompatible with best-effort recording.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5b","T5e"],"criteria":["COH"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.532,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Scope: 'Either the terminal transition waits on the sidecar write, or gate_status exposes whether this job's sidecar is readable yet.'","Non-goals: 'Making sidecar recording non-best-effort in a way that would fail a run whose findings failed to persist; the verdict must still be reported.'","If sidecar writes remain best-effort and a write fails, a terminal transition gated on the sidecar landing would never report the verdict — directly contradicting 'the verdict must still be reported.'"],"finding":"The 'defer the terminal transition until the sidecar lands' solution option in Scope contradicts the Non-goal that the verdict must still be reported even when findings fail to persist.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"faec1c957715e41e7","impact":0.536,"is_primary":null,"location":"Scope + Non-goals","norm_id":"n5d701e34dd42a7c6","priority":0.268,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A run completes but its sidecar write fails permanently; under the defer option the verdict is never surfaced."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"State that if the sidecar write fails/never lands, the verdict is still reported terminal but marked not-readable (favoring the expose-readability option), rather than blocking the terminal transition indefinitely.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.5,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitig